<!--
  <sui-table> — Ship's reference data-grid primitive.

  Three variants on ONE tag:
  - slot   (default): consumer authors <thead>/<tbody> rows in the light DOM;
            the shadow projects them through named slots.
  - native: consumer authors a full <table> in the light DOM; the shadow only
            frames it (no shadow <table>).
  - data:   engine-backed. The headless `createTable()` engine arrives via
            `prop:table={table}` IDENTITY binding (never a serialized object
            attribute); the windowed body renders `table.centerRows()` through a
            createVirtualizer viewport as a CSS grid. `rows`/`columns` string
            props are an SSR/declarative fallback parsed in the controller.

  Density is the platform axis (`<html data-density>`) — rows read the
  `--density-*` channel directly. There is NO `density`/`dense` prop.

  Events (host.emit): sui-sort {key, direction}, sui-sort-change {sorting},
  sui-row-click {id, index}, sui-row-select {id, selected, selectedIds},
  sui-cell-edit {rowId, columnId, value}.

  NEW SURFACE (re-port from feat/next, parity-gate pass)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - No tone prop on this component — rule "tone is global now" doesn't apply.
  - L1 controls were already framework-composed pre-gate (sui-checkbox,
    sui-input, sui-icon, sui-pagination, sui-empty-state) — nothing hand-
    skinned to strip.
  - sx is closed-vocabulary on the two `.empty` divs (slot/native variants);
    the style block keeps the data-variant grid layout, which sx structurally
    cannot express (CSS grid template/auto-columns, position:sticky/absolute,
    pseudo-selectors, @media forced-colors).
  - The variants blocks targeting part=wrap / part=empty (below the props)
    replace the old :host([sticky-header]) display:block-on-.wrap and
    :host([data-empty]) display-toggle raw selectors.
  - Anatomy (light DOM, class-based — part= left on per the wave sweep note):
    .wrap (root frame) > table/.grid (variant switch) > thead/.grid-head,
    tbody/.viewport > .spacer > .grid-row > .grid-cell; .empty (slot/native
    empty state); .grid-empty (data-variant empty state, wraps sui-empty-state).

  LANG-GAP — no space/dimension token in the ~45–179px range
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  The space scale jumps --control-h-xl (44px) → --panel-min-w-sm (180px); the
  data-grid's feat/next column-min-width (80px, `minmax(80px, 1fr)` on both
  `.grid-head` and `.grid-row`) has no home in the closed vocabulary. Snapped
  to the nearest existing token, --space-8 (40px) — a real ~50% reduction in
  the grid's minimum column floor, not a cosmetic rounding. Reported, not
  routed around with a raw px value. (The 40px gutter/checkbox column DOES
  have an exact match, --space-8 — corrected from the prior pass's wrong pick,
  --control-h-md/34px.)

  LANG-GAP (compiler bug) — `sui-css-token` rejects underscore-suffixed
  fine-step space tokens
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  --space-0_75 (3px) is the EXACT match for the selected-row inset rail (was
  3px in feat/next), but referencing it via var() in a style block fails the
  sui-css-token lint: "unknown CSS token --space-0; did you mean --space-4?".
  Root cause (crates/sui/lint/src/rules/css_token.rs `is_ident_cont`): the
  var()-reference scanner's identifier char-class is
  `[a-z0-9-]`, no `_`, so it truncates the name at the underscore
  (`space-0_75` → `space-0`) — while `crate::tokens::registry()`'s
  *declaration* parser (tokens.rs) DOES accept `_`, so the full name is
  correctly registered and simply never matched against. Every other
  fine-step token (--space-1_25, -1_5, -2_5, -3_5, -4_5) silently survives
  this same bug only because its truncated prefix (space-1/-2/-3/-4) happens
  to ALSO be a valid whole-unit token — --space-0_75 is the one family member
  whose truncated prefix (space-0) isn't (by design: "no --space-0 token
  exists; p:0 must mean zero padding, not a var" — tokens.rs). Kept
  --space-half (2px, the prior pass's pick) rather than the exact match — a
  compiler-level bug, not mine to fix; reported, not routed around.

  LANG-GAP (minor) — no exact 0.06em letter-spacing token
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  --tracking-wide is 0.04em, --tracking-wider is 0.1em; feat/next's column-
  header letter-spacing is 0.06em. Snapped to --tracking-wide (closer of the
  two, off by 0.02em vs 0.04em). Cosmetic; noted for completeness.

  LANG-GAP (compiler bug, HIGHER-severity — found authoring THIS comment) —
  `lower_variants` isn't comment-aware
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  crates/sui/compiler/src/parse/preprocess.rs `lower_variants()` finds the
  next real variants block via a raw source scan for the variants open-tag
  prefix and its matching close-tag, with NO HTML-comment skip — unlike its sibling
  lowering passes in the same file, which all explicitly check
  `source[i..].starts_with("<!--")` and skip the comment body verbatim
  (there's even a regression test guarding the identical failure mode for
  element names, "a CSS comment naming <label> swallowed"). Writing this
  component's own doc comment as prose describing its two variants blocks
  (literally spelling the tag out, e.g. a backtick-quoted
  "variants part=wrap" open-tag) made the scanner treat THAT prose mention
  as the block start, walk forward to the real closing tag of the SECOND
  real block, and splice out everything between — including this comment's
  own closing marker — corrupting the file into an "unterminated comment"
  parse error with no useful diagnostic pointing at the real cause. Worked
  around by rephrasing the doc prose to avoid the literal open-tag spelling;
  the underlying scanner gap is unfixed and will bite the next author who
  documents a variants block by example. Compiler-level, not mine to fix;
  reported, not routed around.
-->

<prop name="variant" values="slot|native|data" default="slot" reflect />
<prop name="rows" type="string" default="" />
<prop name="columns" type="string" default="" />
<prop name="hoverable" type="bool" default="true" reflect />
<prop name="striped" type="bool" default="false" reflect />
<prop name="sticky-header" type="bool" default="false" reflect />
<prop name="sticky-first-col" type="bool" default="false" reflect />
<prop name="gutter" type="bool" default="false" reflect />
<prop name="selectable" values="none|single|multi" default="none" reflect />
<prop name="size" values="sm|md|lg" default="md" reflect />
<prop name="label" type="string" default="" />


<variants part="wrap">
  sticky-header: overflow-y:auto
</variants>
<variants part="empty">
  data-empty: display:block
</variants>

<style>
  :host {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--density-text);
    color: var(--foreground);
    --table-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    /* Column count drives the data-variant grid track template; set per render
       from colCount(). Declared here so the value resolves without a fallback. */
    --sui-col-count: 1;
  }
  :host([hidden]) { display: none; }

  .wrap {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--table-radius);
    background: var(--surface-1);
    /* Frost on glass themes (--card-backdrop-filter is `none` elsewhere).
       isolation establishes a stacking context so the backdrop-filter clips to
       --table-radius — works with the existing overflow:hidden. One change
       covers all rows, which render inside .wrap. */
    backdrop-filter: var(--card-backdrop-filter);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: var(--card-backdrop-filter);
    isolation: isolate;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-xs);
    overflow: hidden;
    overflow-x: auto;
    transition: box-shadow var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: separate;
    border-spacing: 0;
    table-layout: auto;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  :host([sticky-header]) .wrap { max-height: inherit; }

  .empty {
    display: none;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* ── Data variant — CSS-grid "table" (windowed center band) ─────────────── */
  .grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    width: 100%;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .grid-head {
    display: grid;
    grid-auto-flow: column;
    grid-auto-columns: minmax(var(--space-8), 1fr);
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: var(--z-sticky);
    background: var(--surface-2);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 0 0 var(--border);
  }
  :host([gutter]) .grid-head,
  :host([gutter]) .grid-row {
    grid-template-columns: var(--space-8) repeat(var(--sui-col-count), minmax(var(--space-8), 1fr));
    grid-auto-flow: row;
    grid-auto-columns: auto;
  }
  .col-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    padding: var(--density-row-py) var(--density-row-px);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    white-space: nowrap;
    user-select: none;
  }
  .col-head[data-sort-key] { cursor: pointer; }
  .col-head[data-sort-key]:hover,
  .col-head[aria-sort='ascending'],
  .col-head[aria-sort='descending'] { color: var(--foreground); }
  .col-head sui-icon { color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .gutter-cell {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0 var(--space-1);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--divider);
    background: var(--surface-2);
  }
  .filter-row {
    padding: var(--space-1) var(--density-row-px) var(--space-2);
  }
  .viewport {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    overflow-y: auto;
    max-height: var(--panel-max-h-md);
  }
  .spacer {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .grid-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-auto-flow: column;
    grid-auto-columns: minmax(var(--space-8), 1fr);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    transition: background-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  :host([hoverable]) .grid-row:hover > .grid-cell { background: var(--hover-bg); }
  .grid-row[data-selected] > .grid-cell { background: var(--selected-bg); }
  .grid-row[data-selected] > .grid-cell:first-child { box-shadow: inset var(--space-half) 0 0 0 var(--primary); }
  .grid-row:focus-visible {
    outline: none;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 var(--ring-width) var(--ring-color);
  }
  .grid-cell {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--density-row-py) var(--density-row-px);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--divider);
    color: var(--foreground);
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .grid-cell.align-right { justify-content: flex-end; }
  .grid-cell.align-center { justify-content: center; }
  .grid-empty {
    padding: var(--space-7) var(--space-5);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .grid-foot {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--density-row-px);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface-2);
  }
  .grid-foot sui-pagination { width: 100%; }

  @media (forced-colors: active) {
    .wrap { border-color: CanvasText; }
    .grid-cell, .col-head { border-bottom-color: CanvasText; }
  }
</style>

{#if variant() === 'data'}
<div class="wrap" part="wrap">
  {#if isEmptyInitial()}
    <div class="grid-empty" part="empty" role="status">
      <sui-empty-state data-empty-initial></sui-empty-state>
    </div>
  {:else if isEmptyFiltered()}
    <div class="grid-empty" part="empty" role="status">
      <sui-empty-state>
        <button slot="action" type="button" data-action="clear-filters">Clear filters</button>
      </sui-empty-state>
    </div>
  {:else}
    <div
      class="grid"
      part="table"
      role="grid"
      aria-label={label() || null}
      aria-rowcount={rowCount()}
      aria-colcount={colCount()}
      aria-multiselectable={selectable() === 'multi' ? 'true' : null}
    >
      <thead class="grid-head" part="thead" role="row" style:--sui-col-count={colCount()}>
        {#if gutter()}
          <div class="gutter-cell" role="columnheader">
            <sui-checkbox data-select-all size="sm"></sui-checkbox>
          </div>
        {/if}
        {#for h of headers() key={h.id}}
          <div
            class="col-head"
            role="columnheader"
            data-sort-key={h.sortKey}
            aria-sort={h.canSort ? h.ariaSort : null}
            tabindex={h.canSort ? '0' : null}
          >
            <span>{h.label}</span>
            {#if h.canSort}
              <sui-icon name={h.caret} size="xs" aria-hidden="true"></sui-icon>
            {/if}
            {#if h.canFilter}
              <span class="filter-row" data-filter-col={h.id}>
                <sui-input
                  type="search"
                  size="sm"
                  variant="ghost"
                  placeholder="Filter…"
                  prop:value={h.filterValue}
                ></sui-input>
              </span>
            {/if}
          </div>
        {/for}
      </thead>

      <div class="viewport" part="tbody" role="rowgroup" bind:this={viewportEl}>
        <div class="spacer" style:height={`${totalSize()}px`}>
          {#for w of windowItems() key={w.key}}
            <div
              class="grid-row"
              role="row"
              data-row-id={w.row.id}
              aria-rowindex={w.index + 1}
              tabindex="-1"
              style:transform={`translateY(${w.start}px)`}
              style:--sui-col-count={colCount()}
            >
              {#if gutter()}
                <div class="gutter-cell" role="gridcell">
                  <sui-checkbox
                    size="sm"
                    data-row-select={w.row.id}
                    prop:disabled={!w.row.selectable}
                  ></sui-checkbox>
                </div>
              {/if}
              {#for c of w.row.cells key={c.columnId}}
                <div class="grid-cell" role="gridcell" class:align-right={c.align === 'right'} class:align-center={c.align === 'center'}>
                  {c.value}
                </div>
              {/for}
            </div>
          {/for}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    {#if hasPagination()}
      <div class="grid-foot" part="foot">
        <sui-pagination
          part="pagination"
          prop:page={pageIndex1()}
          prop:total={rowCount()}
          prop:page-size={pageSize()}
        ></sui-pagination>
      </div>
    {/if}
  {/if}
</div>
{:else if variant() !== 'native'}
<div class="wrap" part="wrap">
  <table part="table" aria-label={label() || null}>
    <thead part="thead"><slot name="head"></slot></thead>
    <tbody part="tbody"><slot></slot></tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="empty" part="empty" role="status" sx="p:7 px:5 text:sm bg:surface-1 fg:muted-foreground">
    <slot name="empty"></slot>
  </div>
</div>
{:else}
<div class="wrap" part="wrap">
  <slot></slot>
  <div class="empty" part="empty" role="status" sx="p:7 px:5 text:sm bg:surface-1 fg:muted-foreground">
    <slot name="empty"></slot>
  </div>
</div>
{/if}
